+### 5.8 conversation_list
+
+When history is enabled and the store can list conversations, the server answers a
+`list_conversations` frame with exactly one `conversation_list` frame. It contains summaries only:
+each row has `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` as ISO strings, and `entryCount`; it contains no
+conversation content or credentials. Rows are newest activity first. When history is disabled or
+the store has no listing capability, the server answers `error` with code `UNSUPPORTED` and never
+uses an empty list to represent an unavailable history.
+([validated by: answers the authenticated user with an ordered ISO conversation list and forwards paging](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L146), [validated by: refuses the list when history is off or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L160))
+
+```json
+{
